        "original_id": "128787c5-107c-5b4e-8c05-9b0e1100adf2",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Makbule Atadan; Mustafa Kemal Atatürk\n- Roles: sister; Turkish army officer; revolutionary; founder; President\n- Places: Republic of Turkey\n- Concepts: secularism; nationalism; Kemalism\n\nFacts:\n- Mustafa Kemal Atatürk was born on 19 May 1881 and later became a Turkish army officer, revolutionary, and the founder of the Republic of Turkey.\n- Makbule Atadan was born in 1885 and was the sister of Mustafa Kemal Atatürk.\n- Mustafa Kemal Atatürk served as the first President of the Republic of Turkey from 1923 until his death in 1938.\n- Mustafa Kemal Atatürk died on 10 November 1938.\n- Makbule Atadan died on 18 January 1956.\n- Mustafa Kemal Atatürk was ideologically a secularist and nationalist, and his policies and theories became known as Kemalism.",
